        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "58cb6b52-9919-52fd-8b06-6e418f992301",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Hans Fallada, John Buchan, Alfred Hitchcock\n- Works: Everyone Dies Alone, Every Man Dies Alone, The 39 Steps\n- Roles: writer, novelist, historian, politician, Governor General of Canada\n- Places: Germany, West Germany, Canada, Scotland\n\nFacts:\n- John Buchan was born on 26 August 1875 and became a Scottish novelist, historian, and Unionist politician.\n- Hans Fallada was born as Rudolf Wilhelm Friedrich Ditzen on 21 July 1893 and was a German writer of the first half of the 20th century.\n- The 39 Steps is a melodrama adapted from John Buchan’s 1915 novel and Alfred Hitchcock’s 1935 film.\n- John Buchan served as Governor General of Canada and was the 15th holder of that office since Canadian Confederation.\n- John Buchan died on 11 February 1940.\n- Hans Fallada died on 5 February 1947.\n- Everyone Dies Alone is a German film that was produced and released in West Germany in 1975.\n- Everyone Dies Alone was adapted from Hans Fallada’s novel Every Man Dies Alone.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
